# Consistent terms

Pick one name for each concept and use it everywhere in that project: prose, tables, figure captions, code, configs, and READMEs. Do not rotate synonyms for variety.

```markdown
<!-- Bad -->
analogue scores, then channels, then columns, then X
y, positives, MoA, labels
node features vs gene features vs scores
signal vs information vs lift

<!-- Good -->
features (the 18 inputs)
labels (clinical-stage mechanisms)
genes (what is ranked)
predictions (model output)
```

Lock a short glossary when a piece of work starts. Example for gene ranking:

| Concept | Use | Do not mix in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Inputs | features | analogue scores, channels, columns (except real dataframe talk) |
| Supervision | labels | y, positives, MoA (as the noun for the label) |
| Ranking unit | genes | nodes (except one sentence on message passing) |
| Model output | predictions | scores (except a proper name: STRING combined score, Open Targets overall) |

If a source already named a field (STRING combined score, Open Targets overall), keep that proper name. Do not invent a parallel nickname beside it.
